  <prompt>Port ValidateDeployedEnvironmentScriptRunner (Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1, 532 lines: az rest x2, az login, pac auth create, Invoke-RestMethod x3 -- probe-style GETs) to C# HttpClient effect probes: BFF /health, sample analysis, doc upload+index, layout render, wizard field-map. Per DS-4 §5/DS-1b §1 (collaborator #25)'s explicit convergence bonus: 'the script port and the placeholder replacement are the SAME WORK DONE ONCE' -- this task should REUSE any HttpClient probe infrastructure already built for tasks 170-180's I2/I4 probes rather than authoring a parallel HTTP-probing helper.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in C# effect-probe authoring against a live BFF (health, analysis, document upload/index, layout render, field-mapping wizard) and converging duplicate probe infrastructure.</role>

  <goal>IE2EValidationRunner exists as a pure C# implementation of the 5 effect probes Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 performs: BFF /health check, a sample AI analysis call, a sample document upload+index round-trip, a workspace-layout render check, and a wizard field-mapping check. It reuses (not duplicates) any HttpClient probe helper infrastructure from tasks 170-180 where applicable (e.g., I4's BFF diagnostic-endpoint call pattern).</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §6's placeholder table lists IE2EValidationRunner's current state as 'pwsh Validate-DeployedEnvironment.ps1 (real script, unrunnable in L2)' -- the script itself is correct, it simply cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site. DS-1b §1 (collaborator #25) explicitly frames this as a convergence bonus with the trap/invariant probe work: 'C3.1/C3.2 already oblige writing 11 real trap/invariant probes in C# (T1 ARM read, T2/T3 Dataverse+Graph, T5 role-assignment read, T6 app-only SPE GET...) -- the script port and the placeholder replacement are the same work done once.'</background>
